    "title": "TCP/IP and Internet Standards Community",
    "summary": "This community centers on TCP/IP, the foundational protocol suite of the Internet, and its relationships with key internet protocols (DNS, HTTP, SMTP) and the Internet Engineering Task Force (IETF). The IETF serves as the primary standards organization responsible for developing and maintaining TCP/IP and related protocols. All application-layer protocols in the community—DNS, HTTP, and SMTP—operate within the TCP/IP architecture, relying on its transport and network layers for functionality.",
